wasivst HARD BLOCKER: v86 (the emulator the whole stack is built on) cannot boot 64-bit kernels. v86 README verbatim: "Linux works pretty well. 64-bit kernels are not supported." It JITs x86 incl. some 64-bit *instructions* but is a 32-bit-kernel machine. Since the product requires 64-bit Wine + 64-bit VST DLLs, v86 is disqualified. Any performance rethink must FIRST replace the emulator (candidates: QEMU-TCG-to-wasm full-system, Box64+Wine-to-wasm userspace, or a long-mode-capable wasm x86-64 emulator like blink). CLAUDE.md and the entire src/worklet v86 path are built on this false premise.